{"id":"st2056","designation":"ST 2056","title":"MPEG TS Packets Carried in VANC","state":"active","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2056/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2056/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This Standard defines a standardized wrapper for the carriage of low bit rate MPEG-2 TS packets, in the 10bit vertical ancillary data (VANC) space of a standard definition or high definition serial digital link in accordance with SMPTE ST 291. Examples of such low bitrate services are EBIF and DVB bitmapped subtitles. Note: Low bit rate means typically 1-20 TS packets per video frame.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Definitions and Acronyms","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 System Overview (Informative)","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Use Cases for MPEG-2 TS in VANC Services (Informative)","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 Breaking the Prior MPEG TS Clock Domain (Informative)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 Additional Considerations for DVB Subtitles (Informative)","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.4 Table Handling (Informative)","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"5.5 Data Carousels (Informative)","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"6 Format of TS Carriage Data Packets","page":6},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 TSCD Structure Syntax","page":7},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 TS Carriage Data Structure Semantics","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.1 PTS_processing_flag: Cases 0 and 1","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.2 PTS_processing_flag: Case 2","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"7 Immediate Placement Messages","page":10},{"level":1,"title":"8 Frame Aligned Placement Messages","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"8.1 DVB Subtitle Streams","page":10},{"level":1,"title":"9 Cyclic Placement Messages","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"9.1 Carousel Removal State","page":11},{"level":1,"title":"10 PSI/SI Ta